1
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:37,527
This is the time known as the Great Pirate Era.

2
00:02:37,827 --> 00:02:41,827
A countless array of pirates go to battle across the seas in search of the One Piece,

3
00:02:42,067 --> 00:02:46,007
the legendary treasure left behind by Golden Roger, King of the Pirates.

4
00:02:46,587 --> 00:02:50,887
Monkey D. Luffy, a boy whose body turned to rubber after eating the gum-gum fruit,

5
00:02:51,167 --> 00:02:53,647
set sail to become the next King of the Pirates.

6
00:02:54,047 --> 00:02:56,627
As Luffy and his crew conquer numerous obstacles,

7
00:02:56,927 --> 00:02:59,747
they capture the unwanted attention of the world government,

8
00:02:59,747 --> 00:03:02,807
which will use any means necessary to stop them.

9
00:03:04,367 --> 00:03:05,707
This sight!

10
00:03:06,787 --> 00:03:09,587
Can't wait to see what kind of adventure's up next!

11
00:03:10,127 --> 00:03:13,167
With a charted course awash in danger and intrigue,

12
00:03:13,387 --> 00:03:17,427
the crew will cut a path across the Grand Line to the New World.

13
00:03:20,887 --> 00:03:25,587
Luffy was sent flying from the Sabaody Archipelago by Bartholomew Kuma.

14
00:03:26,267 --> 00:03:28,147
After soaring through the sky for hours,

15
00:03:28,147 --> 00:03:32,647
he found himself in a kingdom inhabited entirely by women, Amazon Lily.

16
00:03:33,487 --> 00:03:36,827
After a difficult battle, he won the favor of their empress,

17
00:03:37,187 --> 00:03:38,847
a woman named Boa Hancock.

18
00:03:39,207 --> 00:03:43,727
She agreed to take him back to Sabaody on a pirate ship scheduled to leave the next day.

19
00:03:43,727 --> 00:03:44,387
bombust!

20
00:03:44,447 --> 00:03:47,667
cameras

21
00:03:47,787 --> 00:03:48,907
Ren'inion, its' terrible!

22
00:03:48,987 --> 00:03:49,867
Inishida!

23
00:03:49,967 --> 00:03:51,267
what's all the fuss about?!

24
00:03:53,347 --> 00:03:54,107
It's awful.

25
00:03:55,447 --> 00:03:57,127
She's come down with the sickness.

26
00:03:57,987 --> 00:03:59,607
And no one knows what it is.

27
00:03:59,607 --> 00:04:07,407
You're a damned fool, Boa Hancock

28
00:04:07,407 --> 00:04:13,907
Empress or not, one does not simply ignore a summons from the world government

29
00:04:13,907 --> 00:04:18,347
The weight of your pride is going to sink your entire nation

30
00:04:18,347 --> 00:04:23,727
If we don't recognize you as a warlord of the sea, your position as their ruler is meaningless

31
00:04:23,727 --> 00:04:28,807
Love is a hurricane, love love Hancock

32
00:04:29,607 --> 00:04:35,467
Whatever it is, fight it!

33
00:04:35,467 --> 00:04:36,627
Don't give up

34
00:04:36,627 --> 00:04:42,427
What's this about the snake princess falling ill?

35
00:04:43,427 --> 00:04:44,767
Oh, Gran and Yon

36
00:04:44,767 --> 00:04:51,587
Man, I need you to wait outside

37
00:04:51,587 --> 00:04:54,447
What? But why? I'm in a hurry

38
00:04:54,447 --> 00:04:55,387
I know that!

39
00:04:59,607 --> 00:05:02,347
It hurts

40
00:05:02,347 --> 00:05:06,047
She keeps clutching her chest

41
00:05:06,047 --> 00:05:08,467
Perhaps something is wrong with her heart

42
00:05:08,467 --> 00:05:15,187
I've never seen anything like it

43
00:05:15,187 --> 00:05:20,467
Since her symptoms are a mystery, there's very little I can do in terms of treatment

44
00:05:20,467 --> 00:05:23,567
All we know is that it's extremely painful

45
00:05:23,567 --> 00:05:26,327
She won't eat a thing and she's hardly speaking either

46
00:05:26,327 --> 00:05:35,747
I'll be out of here tomorrow morning

47
00:05:35,747 --> 00:05:38,627
Soon we're all gonna be back together

48
00:05:38,627 --> 00:05:41,947
Tomorrow morning

49
00:05:41,947 --> 00:05:44,427
It's as I feared

50
00:05:44,427 --> 00:05:48,867
What are you doing?

51
00:05:48,867 --> 00:05:51,467
Whatever it is, Gran and Yon, you've got to stop it!

52
00:05:51,467 --> 00:05:53,707
Can't you see you're hurting her with this nonsense?

53
00:05:53,707 --> 00:05:55,907
Do you want to get to the bottom of this or not?

54
00:05:55,907 --> 00:05:59,907
Ugh, yes, of course

55
00:05:59,907 --> 00:06:02,867
That fool, I should have realized

56
00:06:02,867 --> 00:06:07,047
It's a pity that the virus came at a time like this

57
00:06:07,047 --> 00:06:08,247
Huh? Virus?

58
00:06:08,247 --> 00:06:10,667
If you know what it is, then just tell us

59
00:06:10,667 --> 00:06:13,167
I can't breathe, Gran and Yon

60
00:06:13,167 --> 00:06:17,667
Am I going to die like this?

61
00:06:17,667 --> 00:06:20,507
Indeed, yes

62
00:06:20,507 --> 00:06:22,027
I'll say it isn't so!

63
00:06:22,087 --> 00:06:24,727
If this is supposed to be a joke, we're not laughing!

64
00:06:25,327 --> 00:06:27,007
It has killed us before

65
00:06:27,007 --> 00:06:30,067
It took the life of our last Empress

66
00:06:30,067 --> 00:06:35,347
The same fate befell the Empress before her, too

67
00:06:35,347 --> 00:06:37,587
I suffered from the illness myself

68
00:06:37,587 --> 00:06:39,987
But left the country before it took my life

69
00:06:39,987 --> 00:06:41,947
No remedy could save me

70
00:06:41,947 --> 00:06:46,307
Snake Princess, Monkey Diluffi has come to see you as well

71
00:06:46,307 --> 00:06:47,967
This is hardly the time

72
00:06:47,967 --> 00:06:50,067
He has a request to ask of you

73
00:06:50,067 --> 00:06:51,567
Will you hear it?

74
00:06:51,747 --> 00:06:53,227
What do you mean, request?

75
00:06:53,327 --> 00:06:54,547
Can't you see she's suffering?

76
00:06:54,907 --> 00:06:56,187
How important could it be?

77
00:06:56,407 --> 00:06:56,667
Oh!

78
00:06:57,387 --> 00:06:58,687
What just happened?

79
00:06:59,367 --> 00:07:00,227
Show him in

80
00:07:00,227 --> 00:07:01,467
Quickly

81
00:07:01,467 --> 00:07:13,467
Monkey Diluffi, you are a man favored by fate

82
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:16,467
Perhaps this mountain can be moved after all

83
00:07:16,467 --> 00:07:19,467
And perhaps you are the one to do it

84
00:07:19,467 --> 00:07:22,307
I hear you need something?

85
00:07:24,427 --> 00:07:25,807
Yeah, I sure do!

86
00:07:26,407 --> 00:07:28,467
But are you okay? I heard you were sick

87
00:07:28,467 --> 00:07:29,627
Never mind that

88
00:07:29,627 --> 00:07:31,627
No illness can overtake me

89
00:07:31,627 --> 00:07:37,827
There's a pirate on Whitebeard's crew named Ace

90
00:07:37,827 --> 00:07:40,147
He's my brother and he's about to be executed

91
00:07:40,147 --> 00:07:41,967
I gotta go rescue him

92
00:07:41,967 --> 00:07:45,247
But I heard if we took a pirate ship, it'd be too slow

93
00:07:45,247 --> 00:07:47,907
That man is your brother?

94
00:07:48,287 --> 00:07:49,947
Do you mean Fire Fist, Ace?

95
00:07:50,347 --> 00:07:50,827
Exactly!

96
00:07:51,127 --> 00:07:52,967
So instead of going back to my friends

97
00:07:52,967 --> 00:07:56,007
I need you to get on a Navy ship and take me with you!

98
00:07:56,007 --> 00:07:59,887
How dare you even suggest that, you selfish beast?

99
00:08:00,347 --> 00:08:03,107
You know full well the horrors our poor sister went through

100
00:08:03,107 --> 00:08:05,687
And still you would drag her to that abhorrent prison?

101
00:08:07,347 --> 00:08:08,947
How can you be so cruel?

102
00:08:09,067 --> 00:08:11,007
This is exactly why we hate men

103
00:08:11,007 --> 00:08:12,627
We very well could have killed you

104
00:08:12,627 --> 00:08:14,007
But as soon as we show you mercy

105
00:08:14,007 --> 00:08:15,447
Then you let it go to your head

106
00:08:15,447 --> 00:08:18,207
You're lucky she doesn't turn you to stone and smash you

107
00:08:18,207 --> 00:08:19,887
You want me to follow the government's orders

108
00:08:19,887 --> 00:08:22,387
And go with the other warlords?

109
00:08:23,927 --> 00:08:25,047
He's said enough!

110
00:08:25,367 --> 00:08:26,527
Strike him down!

111
00:08:27,627 --> 00:08:29,647
If that is truly your request

112
00:08:29,647 --> 00:08:31,467
Then of course

113
00:08:31,467 --> 00:08:34,207
I will go anywhere you like

114
00:08:34,207 --> 00:08:38,947
Whoa, thanks!

115
00:08:39,067 --> 00:08:39,927
I was worried!

116
00:08:40,307 --> 00:08:42,107
I don't know what I would have done without your help!

117
00:08:42,107 --> 00:08:44,267
She actually said yes

118
00:08:44,267 --> 00:08:46,007
She wouldn't listen to reason

119
00:08:46,007 --> 00:08:47,327
But she'll listen to him!

120
00:08:47,327 --> 00:08:48,727
What happened to her granny?

121
00:08:48,887 --> 00:08:50,607
Like the Empress before her

122
00:08:50,607 --> 00:08:54,147
Our Empress succumbed to the burning flames

123
00:08:54,147 --> 00:08:56,307
That are known only as love

124
00:08:56,307 --> 00:09:00,607
There's a saying in the East Blue

125
00:09:00,607 --> 00:09:02,567
That describes these winds of passion

126
00:09:02,567 --> 00:09:07,427
Love is always a miracle!

127
00:09:07,427 --> 00:09:21,827
Heavens, my heart is a flutter

128
00:09:21,827 --> 00:09:25,307
I feel I might do anything Luffy asks of me

129
00:09:25,307 --> 00:09:28,347
I acquiesce without a second thought

130
00:09:28,347 --> 00:09:30,307
And I don't regret it

131
00:09:30,307 --> 00:09:31,407
Not even the slightest

132
00:09:31,407 --> 00:09:33,367
That's what they call love

133
00:09:33,367 --> 00:09:34,487
Love?

134
00:09:34,947 --> 00:09:36,807
Once it has a hold on your heart

135
00:09:36,807 --> 00:09:38,287
It will squeeze and squeeze

136
00:09:38,287 --> 00:09:39,507
Until you fall over dead

137
00:09:39,507 --> 00:09:41,767
If you cannot be with the one you desire

138
00:09:41,767 --> 00:09:44,327
The Empresses that came before you

139
00:09:44,327 --> 00:09:46,487
All fell in love with men as well

140
00:09:46,487 --> 00:09:48,747
But as they were unable to leave their kingdom

141
00:09:48,747 --> 00:09:50,947
They were forced to bottle up their feelings

142
00:09:50,947 --> 00:09:52,287
While they stayed

143
00:09:52,287 --> 00:09:54,047
Their heartache grew and grew

144
00:09:54,047 --> 00:09:55,867
Until the pain was so great

145
00:09:55,867 --> 00:09:57,367
That they died from sorrow

146
00:09:57,367 --> 00:10:01,087
Little did you know

147
00:10:01,087 --> 00:10:02,867
That by agreeing to his request

148
00:10:02,867 --> 00:10:04,767
You may have saved your own life

149
00:10:04,767 --> 00:10:07,607
Although you were struck with lovesickness

150
00:10:07,607 --> 00:10:09,407
If Luffy had not arrived

151
00:10:09,407 --> 00:10:11,027
And requested this very thing

152
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:13,307
You would have lost your title as warlord

153
00:10:13,307 --> 00:10:15,067
And led this kingdom to ruin

154
00:10:15,067 --> 00:10:18,047
However, one may say

155
00:10:18,047 --> 00:10:20,167
That he is just as fortunate as you

156
00:10:20,167 --> 00:10:21,267
After all

157
00:10:21,267 --> 00:10:23,427
Had fate not brought him to this island

158
00:10:23,427 --> 00:10:25,687
The only way he could hope to enter that prison

159
00:10:25,687 --> 00:10:26,887
Would be in chains

160
00:10:26,887 --> 00:10:28,307
Just like his brother

161
00:10:28,307 --> 00:10:35,847
Hello, Momonga

162
00:10:35,847 --> 00:10:38,947
Is this Boa Hancock?

163
00:10:39,227 --> 00:10:40,787
Yes, and I have decided to honor

164
00:10:40,787 --> 00:10:42,707
That little request of yours after all

165
00:10:42,707 --> 00:10:45,447
However, there is one condition

166
00:10:45,447 --> 00:10:46,767
That must be met first

167
00:10:46,767 --> 00:10:47,707
Yes?

168
00:10:47,947 --> 00:10:49,447
Naturally, if you can't accept

169
00:10:49,447 --> 00:10:51,767
You might as well turn your boat around and leave

170
00:10:51,767 --> 00:10:55,567
All right, enough suspense then

171
00:10:55,567 --> 00:10:57,567
Let me hear it

172
00:10:57,567 --> 00:11:12,547
I thought he wasn't leaving the kingdom until tomorrow though

173
00:11:12,547 --> 00:11:14,707
I heard there was a last minute change of plans

174
00:11:14,707 --> 00:11:17,947
Now he's getting on a navy ship along with a snake princess

175
00:11:17,947 --> 00:11:19,267
Hi Luffy

176
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:21,007
Hey guys, thanks for everything

177
00:11:21,007 --> 00:11:21,827
This was fun

178
00:11:21,827 --> 00:11:24,747
I'll come back to visit and bring my friends next time

179
00:11:24,747 --> 00:11:25,687
Your pirate crew?

180
00:11:25,827 --> 00:11:28,767
Yeah, I bet our chef would be totally crazy about this place

181
00:11:28,767 --> 00:11:30,587
He likes girls so much it's scary

182
00:11:30,587 --> 00:11:32,007
Oh, but his food is awesome

183
00:11:32,007 --> 00:11:32,687
I promise

184
00:11:32,687 --> 00:11:34,747
I bet he'd love to cook for you

185
00:11:34,747 --> 00:11:37,427
Our musician's awesome too

186
00:11:37,427 --> 00:11:38,347
He's a skeleton

187
00:11:38,347 --> 00:11:39,467
A skeleton?

188
00:11:39,807 --> 00:11:40,627
His name's Brooke

189
00:11:40,627 --> 00:11:41,367
But watch out

190
00:11:41,367 --> 00:11:42,567
Because as soon as he meets you

191
00:11:42,567 --> 00:11:44,287
He's going to want to check out your panties

192
00:11:44,287 --> 00:11:45,087
Our panties?

193
00:11:45,327 --> 00:11:46,507
I have lots to show him

194
00:11:46,507 --> 00:11:47,787
But I don't see the appeal

195
00:11:47,787 --> 00:11:51,207
And we've got this little reindeer doctor named Chopper too

196
00:11:51,207 --> 00:11:56,627
They're all guys

197
00:11:56,627 --> 00:11:57,927
Except Nami and Robin

198
00:11:57,927 --> 00:11:59,827
But it's no fun if we can't all visit

199
00:11:59,827 --> 00:12:02,707
Even if men are forbidden here

200
00:12:02,707 --> 00:12:03,847
I think they'll make an exception

201
00:12:03,847 --> 00:12:06,087
The snake princess seems to favor you

202
00:12:06,087 --> 00:12:08,527
So it's not likely that they would be sentenced to death

203
00:12:08,527 --> 00:12:10,107
Well, probably not at least

204
00:12:10,107 --> 00:12:14,227
And there's our empress now

205
00:12:14,227 --> 00:12:19,387
Who had the audacity to place these beasts in my path?

206
00:12:21,467 --> 00:12:21,987
Detestable

207
00:12:21,987 --> 00:12:24,787
Beastlessly adorable obstacles

208
00:12:24,787 --> 00:12:29,707
We love you, princess

209
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:32,027
If I was half the sexiest, sir

210
00:12:32,027 --> 00:12:33,687
I'd spend all day in front of a mirror

211
00:12:33,687 --> 00:12:35,787
She's even more striking than usual

212
00:12:35,787 --> 00:12:37,587
I didn't think that was possible

213
00:12:37,587 --> 00:12:39,047
My deepest apologies

214
00:12:39,047 --> 00:12:40,907
I accept full responsibility

215
00:12:40,907 --> 00:12:43,347
You should be more careful

216
00:12:43,347 --> 00:12:46,187
Hey, looks like you're feeling all better

217
00:12:46,187 --> 00:12:52,227
Hate to be rude, but we gotta hurry, snake lady

218
00:12:52,227 --> 00:12:54,247
I can't look him in the eye

219
00:12:54,247 --> 00:12:55,107
It's too much

220
00:12:55,107 --> 00:12:56,687
That's rude, Luffy

221
00:12:56,687 --> 00:12:58,667
You can't call her snake lady

222
00:12:58,667 --> 00:12:59,947
It's snake princess

223
00:12:59,947 --> 00:13:01,187
Don't forget it

224
00:13:01,187 --> 00:13:05,807
You can simply call me Hancock if you like

225
00:13:05,807 --> 00:13:08,507
You're so cute

226
00:13:08,507 --> 00:13:09,307
Cool

227
00:13:09,307 --> 00:13:11,267
Whatever works for you, hammock

228
00:13:11,267 --> 00:13:13,107
It's, uh, Hancock

229
00:13:13,107 --> 00:13:15,567
The snake princess just smiled at me

230
00:13:15,567 --> 00:13:16,567
It's like a diamond

231
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:18,807
No, it's like the stars in the sky

232
00:13:18,807 --> 00:13:20,107
I'm dazzled

233
00:13:20,107 --> 00:13:21,867
The spark of a woman in love

234
00:13:21,867 --> 00:13:24,667
It makes me long for the sweet days of my youth

235
00:13:24,667 --> 00:13:24,987
Why?

236
00:13:25,207 --> 00:13:26,507
Is something wrong, Granny Young?

237
00:13:26,587 --> 00:13:28,347
Your face is looking rather grotesque

238
00:13:28,347 --> 00:13:29,627
How dare you?

239
00:13:34,267 --> 00:13:35,987
Have a safe trip, snake princess

240
00:13:35,987 --> 00:13:37,447
We'll miss you, Luffy

241
00:13:37,447 --> 00:13:38,447
We'll miss you, Luffy

242
00:13:38,447 --> 00:13:39,447
Come back soon

243
00:13:39,447 --> 00:13:41,447
Bye-bye

244
00:13:41,447 --> 00:13:43,027
Would you stop that?

245
00:13:43,027 --> 00:13:43,447
Bye-bye

246
00:13:43,447 --> 00:13:49,947
We're serious about you coming back

247
00:13:49,947 --> 00:13:53,447
Indeed, we'll await your return with faded breath

248
00:13:53,447 --> 00:14:10,907
I had no obligation to save you

249
00:14:10,907 --> 00:14:14,087
This is great

250
00:14:14,087 --> 00:14:16,287
I was really freaking out there

251
00:14:16,287 --> 00:14:17,947
I thought you guys were gonna die

252
00:14:17,947 --> 00:14:31,987
Hey, Luffy

253
00:14:31,987 --> 00:14:34,447
I hope you get to see your friends soon

254
00:14:34,447 --> 00:14:35,447
Thanks

255
00:14:35,447 --> 00:14:41,147
Granny Neon

256
00:14:41,147 --> 00:14:41,707
Huh?

257
00:14:42,067 --> 00:14:45,347
I'm not worried about the snake princess reaching the prison unharmed

258
00:14:45,347 --> 00:14:47,587
But how will she manage to bring Luffy with her?

259
00:14:48,447 --> 00:14:52,467
Well, it will require some trickery, I can say that

260
00:14:52,467 --> 00:14:56,047
The man has a 300 million berry bounty on his head

261
00:14:56,047 --> 00:15:00,887
And I'm certain that the navy is eager to apprehend him after what happened on Saba-Odi

262
00:15:00,887 --> 00:15:04,107
But she can't very well stow him in the cargo

263
00:15:04,107 --> 00:15:06,387
You need to worry

264
00:15:06,387 --> 00:15:11,347
I thought up an excellent strategy and our princess can be quite persuasive

265
00:15:26,047 --> 00:15:42,767
You certainly kept us waiting, Empress

266
00:15:42,767 --> 00:15:45,387
In fact, I'd almost lost hope

267
00:15:45,387 --> 00:15:50,747
Can you guarantee that you'll honor the promise you made earlier?

268
00:15:51,747 --> 00:15:53,827
I contacted my superiors

269
00:15:53,827 --> 00:15:57,167
As long as we're quick about it, we can stop by Impel Down

270
00:15:57,167 --> 00:16:03,547
To be clear, only you and your snake may board

271
00:16:03,547 --> 00:16:06,967
Unless they're shackled, pirates are not welcome at the prison

272
00:16:06,967 --> 00:16:08,327
Warlord or no

273
00:16:08,327 --> 00:16:10,547
They'll make an exception once

274
00:16:10,547 --> 00:16:11,827
But know this

275
00:16:11,827 --> 00:16:13,807
They'll watch you like a hawk

276
00:16:13,807 --> 00:16:15,867
You can't intimidate me

277
00:16:15,867 --> 00:16:20,087
Whatever you do, please try to stay safe

278
00:16:20,087 --> 00:16:22,327
Strike down all who oppose you, sister

279
00:16:22,327 --> 00:16:25,667
Good luck in the battle with Whitebeard, Snake Princess

280
00:16:25,667 --> 00:16:28,047
Luffy, I hope you...

281
00:16:28,047 --> 00:16:32,947
I shall return soon

282
00:16:32,947 --> 00:16:35,187
Guard the kingdom in my absence

283
00:16:35,187 --> 00:16:36,207
Of course!

284
00:16:39,927 --> 00:16:41,487
I'm glad I stuck around

285
00:16:41,487 --> 00:16:45,207
I feared I might have to return to headquarters of failure

286
00:16:45,207 --> 00:16:50,927
You were so adamant in your refusal when last we spoke

287
00:16:50,927 --> 00:16:54,207
So you'll forgive me if I ask what happened to change your mind

288
00:16:54,207 --> 00:16:58,587
Hold your tongue all you like

289
00:16:58,587 --> 00:17:00,787
But it seems your stomach will still speak

290
00:17:00,787 --> 00:17:03,467
Even the great pirate empress is only human

291
00:17:03,467 --> 00:17:04,867
How dare you

292
00:17:04,867 --> 00:17:07,767
A lady such as myself would never do something so crass

293
00:17:07,767 --> 00:17:08,907
There's no one else here

294
00:17:08,907 --> 00:17:10,087
Of course not

295
00:17:10,087 --> 00:17:14,907
Luffy, I'm sorry

296
00:17:14,907 --> 00:17:19,107
I didn't eat enough at the banquet with all those girls cheesing me around and touching me

297
00:17:19,107 --> 00:17:21,527
Regardless, if we get caught here, it's all over

298
00:17:21,527 --> 00:17:23,567
I'll ask for food later, I promise

299
00:17:23,567 --> 00:17:25,287
Just tell your stomach to be patient

300
00:17:25,287 --> 00:17:25,847
Got it

301
00:17:25,847 --> 00:17:28,947
And Luffy, it's difficult to walk like this

302
00:17:28,947 --> 00:17:36,407
You don't have a fever, do you?

303
00:17:36,407 --> 00:17:37,767
You're quite flushed

304
00:17:37,767 --> 00:17:39,167
No, everything is fine

305
00:17:39,167 --> 00:17:46,967
Well, while you're here, do you think you can change back my crew members that you turned to stone?

306
00:17:47,427 --> 00:17:52,067
It would be shameful to show up at Navy headquarters in this unsightly state

307
00:17:52,067 --> 00:17:55,507
They are alive, aren't they?

308
00:17:58,947 --> 00:18:01,407
That sneeze, it sounded like a man was...

309
00:18:01,407 --> 00:18:01,947
It was me!

310
00:18:05,227 --> 00:18:05,667
Achoo!

311
00:18:05,987 --> 00:18:07,567
This wind is bad for your health

312
00:18:07,567 --> 00:18:09,407
I may be catching a cold

313
00:18:09,407 --> 00:18:13,487
Sorry, I'm trying to be quiet but your hair tickled my nose

314
00:18:13,487 --> 00:18:15,547
It's alright, I don't think he's on to us

315
00:18:15,547 --> 00:18:17,187
I don't know what it is yet

316
00:18:17,187 --> 00:18:21,407
But you're up to something and I swear I'll get to the bottom of it

317
00:18:21,407 --> 00:18:23,827
Would you care to elaborate?

318
00:18:25,007 --> 00:18:27,447
Aside from the fact that you're acting highly suspicious

319
00:18:27,447 --> 00:18:30,487
Your demeanor is completely different than when I met with you before

320
00:18:30,487 --> 00:18:31,367
We're screwed

321
00:18:31,367 --> 00:18:35,067
I assure you, I have nothing to hide in either body or mind

322
00:18:35,067 --> 00:18:40,047
But if you have any doubts, then I would encourage you to search me yourself if you think you are capable

323
00:18:40,047 --> 00:18:44,747
Well then, what shall it be?

324
00:18:48,787 --> 00:18:51,827
What the heck do you think you're doing? He's gonna find me!

325
00:18:51,827 --> 00:19:01,667
No

326
00:19:01,667 --> 00:19:05,047
If you insist, there's no reason to doubt your word

327
00:19:05,047 --> 00:19:08,327
But I will have to ask you to fix my crew

328
00:19:08,327 --> 00:19:13,207
We can scarcely operate the ship, let alone make your little trip to impel down

329
00:19:13,207 --> 00:19:15,827
Awaken

330
00:19:15,827 --> 00:19:16,927
Awaken

331
00:19:16,927 --> 00:19:26,587
Huh? What happened?

332
00:19:26,587 --> 00:19:27,847
Get ready for departure!

333
00:19:28,327 --> 00:19:29,107
Yes, sir!

334
00:19:29,347 --> 00:19:29,927
Right away!

335
00:19:32,507 --> 00:19:36,167
We'll make a stop at impel down before we return to Marineford

336
00:19:36,167 --> 00:19:45,947
Fleet Admiral Sengoku! We have word from Vice Admiral Momunga!

337
00:19:46,827 --> 00:19:47,307
Huh?

338
00:19:48,527 --> 00:19:51,087
Snake Princess Boa Hancock came to speak with them again

339
00:19:51,087 --> 00:19:52,927
She finally agreed to our conditions

340
00:19:52,927 --> 00:19:54,887
I am told that they're on their way now

341
00:19:54,887 --> 00:19:56,707
It's about time

342
00:19:56,707 --> 00:19:58,667
Let's just hope they're not late

343
00:19:58,667 --> 00:20:01,047
That woman is quite formidable

344
00:20:01,047 --> 00:20:05,307
Now we'll have six of the seven warlords with us

345
00:20:05,307 --> 00:20:07,727
Hawkeye Mihawk

346
00:20:07,727 --> 00:20:10,247
Bartholomew Kuma

347
00:20:10,247 --> 00:20:13,407
Don Quixote Doflamingo

348
00:20:13,407 --> 00:20:15,167
Gekko Moria

349
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:17,667
Marshall D. Teach

350
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:20,407
And Boa Hancock

351
00:20:20,407 --> 00:20:22,747
And the seventh?

352
00:20:22,747 --> 00:20:25,187
Did a little time in prison cool his head?

353
00:20:25,527 --> 00:20:27,467
Perhaps he's ready to aid in our fight now

354
00:20:27,467 --> 00:20:28,387
No, sir!

355
00:20:28,907 --> 00:20:31,647
Just as before, he's adamantly refusing to fight

356
00:20:31,647 --> 00:20:35,427
He went so far as to say he would relinquish his title as warlord

357
00:20:35,427 --> 00:20:40,487
Given his disposition, I had assumed that he would be the most cooperative of the bunch

358
00:20:40,487 --> 00:20:43,707
This is not the time to get hung up on principle

359
00:20:43,707 --> 00:20:45,947
We need you, Team Bay

360
00:20:45,947 --> 00:20:50,007
Fleet Admiral, sir!

361
00:20:50,007 --> 00:20:51,567
Sir, I have an announcement

362
00:20:51,567 --> 00:20:56,867
We have a small issue with the 500 pirates that Admiral Kizaru captured at Sabaori

363
00:20:56,867 --> 00:21:00,507
That is to say, the staff had impelled down so they can't hold them

364
00:21:00,507 --> 00:21:01,967
Send them to a labor camp

365
00:21:01,967 --> 00:21:06,567
Frankly, if it doesn't have to do with Whitebeard, I just don't have time for it right now

366
00:21:06,567 --> 00:21:10,387
I understand, sir, but St. Roswald is, uh...

367
00:21:10,387 --> 00:21:12,527
Let the admirals handle it for once

368
00:21:12,527 --> 00:21:14,327
And where the hell is Garp?

369
00:21:14,327 --> 00:21:18,447
Uh, I already informed you, sir, but he left for impelled down quite some time ago

370
00:21:18,447 --> 00:21:24,767
I guess I should expect that kind of behavior from that old bastard, but not before a battle

371
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:25,807
Excuse me, sir

372
00:21:25,807 --> 00:21:27,787
I'm afraid we have a situation

373
00:21:27,787 --> 00:21:29,487
Whitebeard's ship is advancing

374
00:21:29,487 --> 00:21:31,027
I see

375
00:21:31,027 --> 00:21:33,067
I assume the guard ships are on the line?

376
00:21:33,467 --> 00:21:35,407
Put me through, I'd rather speak to them directly

377
00:21:35,407 --> 00:21:36,527
I can't do that

378
00:21:36,527 --> 00:21:36,907
Huh?

379
00:21:37,307 --> 00:21:38,627
We lost contact, sir

380
00:21:38,627 --> 00:21:43,167
With all 23 Navy vessels keeping tabs on Whitebeard's main ship, the Moby Dick

381
00:21:43,167 --> 00:21:47,527
Given the circumstances, we can only conclude they were eliminated by the enemy

382
00:21:47,527 --> 00:21:50,587
Surely not the whole fleet

383
00:21:50,587 --> 00:21:55,127
There's been some worrying activity from other pirate ships in the New World as well

384
00:21:55,127 --> 00:22:00,967
Without guard ships, we won't have any idea how many ships the enemy is sending or when he's sending them

385
00:22:00,967 --> 00:22:04,167
I've arranged for replacements, but we're in the dark right now

386
00:22:04,167 --> 00:22:08,067
We've been had

387
00:22:08,067 --> 00:22:10,507
I didn't think they would act so quickly

388
00:22:10,507 --> 00:22:14,627
Until new ships are in place, we're flying blind

389
00:22:14,627 --> 00:22:19,747
As long as Ace is there, they may even have the audacity to strike impelled down

390
00:22:19,747 --> 00:22:21,367
So be ready for anything

391
00:22:21,367 --> 00:22:22,307
Yes, sir

392
00:22:22,307 --> 00:22:30,067
Vice Admiral, it will be right this way

393
00:22:30,067 --> 00:22:32,547
Please, be careful

394
00:22:32,547 --> 00:22:33,507
Sure

395
00:22:33,507 --> 00:22:45,107
You're a right mess, boy

396
00:22:45,107 --> 00:22:46,827
I hate to see it

397
00:22:46,827 --> 00:22:56,287
You still breathing in there?

398
00:22:56,287 --> 00:23:00,287
Ace

399
00:23:00,287 --> 00:23:12,267
Sent flying across the world by Kuma, the Straw Hats awaken in strange new places

400
00:23:12,267 --> 00:23:17,107
Nami meets a peculiar old man on a secluded island where a unique science is studied

401
00:23:17,107 --> 00:23:21,467
And Frankie finds himself in a frozen land with no cola in sight

402
00:23:21,467 --> 00:23:27,527
On the next One Piece, the friend's whereabouts, the science of weather and the mechanical island

403
00:23:27,527 --> 00:23:29,647
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

